  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of what these files establish for the impact report:\n\n**Detection logic (Spring Boot side):** `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory` (in `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java`) gates on presence of `org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory` (i.e., `log4j-core`, not `log4j-api` or `log4j-to-slf4j`), registered via `LoggingSystemFactory` + `DelegatingLoggingSystemFactory`/`SpringFactoriesLoader`.\n\n**Bridge modules (Log4j2 side):** `log4j-to-slf4j` (routes Log4j2 API calls \u2192 SLF4J, depends on `log4j-api` + `slf4j-api`) is mutually exclusive with `log4j-slf4j-impl`/`log4j-slf4j2-impl` (routes SLF4J calls \u2192 Log4j2 API), enforced at runtime in `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory`/`Log4jLoggerFactory` via classpath checks that throw `IllegalStateException`/`LoggingException` if both are present.\n\n**Bridge restructuring artifact:** `log4j-spring-boot` module ships its own `Log4j2SpringBootLoggingSystem` (extends Spring's `Log4J2LoggingSystem`) with a `spring.factories` entry \u2014 an override path that competes with Spring Boot's own factory via `@Order` precedence, relevant to how the two projects' logging-system selection can diverge.\n\n**Dependency chain evidence:** `log4j-bom/pom.xml` and `spring-boot-starter-log4j2/build.gradle` pin the actual bridge versions Spring Boot pulls in; `logging.adoc` documents the starter-swap mechanism (`spring-boot-starter-logging` \u2192 `spring-boot-starter-log4j2`).",
